cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the Anchor-Align method, please cite the paper below."
title: "Anchor-Align: Generalizable VLA Finetuning via Representation Anchoring and Language-Action Alignment"
abstract: >-
  Anchor-Align is a finetuning method for vision-language-action (VLA) models that
  prevents behavior cloning from overwriting the pretrained vision-language
  representations supporting visual and semantic generalization. It augments BC with
  Vision-Language Anchoring, which distills layer-wise representations from a frozen
  VLM copy, and Language-Action Alignment, which converts each action target into a
  discrete motion-direction label and jointly trains language and action prediction on
  the same robot observation.
type: software
license: MIT
